@prefix kgjd: <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/data/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

#################################################################
# Confirmed employer -> Wikidata matches
#
# Hand-maintained, NOT regenerated. Every entry here was proposed by
# scripts/match_employer_wikidata.py and reviewed against Wikidata's P31
# (instance of) values before being added -- a candidate is only recorded
# when Wikidata's item is actually typed as an organization/company/business
# and clearly is the employer itself, not a related product, subsidiary, or
# service. scripts/generate.py and scripts/live_records.py merge these
# owl:sameAs links onto matching kgjobs:Employer resources at build time,
# but only for employers actually present in that run's data.
#
# Do not add an entry here without running the match script and checking
# its ORG-TYPED output first. See README.md for the full workflow.
#################################################################

kgjd:employer-openai owl:sameAs <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q21708200> .
# Q21708200 "OpenAI" -- instance of: enterprise. Official website matches
# (https://openai.com/) exactly.

kgjd:employer-accenture owl:sameAs <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q338825> .
# Q338825 "Accenture" -- instance of: business, public company. Official
# website matches (https://www.accenture.com/) exactly.

kgjd:employer-oclc owl:sameAs <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q190593> .
# Q190593 "OCLC, Inc." -- instance of: cooperative, nonprofit organization.
# Official website matches (https://www.oclc.org/) exactly. Note: Wikidata's
# search also surfaces Q846596 "WorldCat" (OCLC's catalog product) typed
# generically as "organization" -- that is a different entity from the
# employer and was deliberately not used here.

# Neo4j (kgjd:employer-neo4j) deliberately has NO entry: Wikidata has no
# item for the Neo4j company, only for the software product (Q1628290,
# typed as proprietary software / graph database / free software, never as
# an organization). Recording owl:sameAs to the product item would wrongly
# assert the employer and the software are the same entity.
